welcome to max tech and this is our  review of the ipad air 5.  i've been using the new ipad air 5 for  two weeks now and i think i finally  gathered my thoughts on where it stands  within the ipad lineup as well as how it  compares to other android tablets on the  market so what i'm gonna do in this  review is talk about how good of an  upgrade this year's ipad air truly is  the disappointments and frustrations  that i have with it and finally my  thoughts on if you should hold off until  the next update of the ipad air which  could actually come with an oled display  for the first time ever but before i get  into all of those juicy leaks i've got  to talk about the ipad air 5 and what i  honestly think about it so i'm just  going to go ahead and call it what it is  a stopgap product yes of course it's an  excellent update since the price is  still the same  599 dollars as before and you're getting  a bunch of spec upgrades and features  but i've got to admit that it feels like  something major is missing and speaking  of those upgrades the biggest one is of  course the new m1 chip which is the same  one that's inside of the ipad pro and  it's much faster than the a14 in the  previous ipad air 4. for example the  single core performance is 7 percent  higher which means that a lot of common  tasks like web browsing or many  different apps will be a bit more snappy  than before but then looking at the  multi-core performance we have a huge  improvement of 69 percent which is gonna  matter for all the high-end productivity  apps that require lots of multi-core  performance but the biggest difference  is when we take a look at the graphics  performance with the m1 chip being 77  faster than the old a14 and this right  here is what matters the most because a  lot of different apps and games depend  on the gpu performance so this means  that it can essentially handle any app  or game out there without missing a beat  no matter if his gentian impact or  anything else it's just gonna be solid  and making things even better we tested  3dmark's wildlife extreme benchmark  which is an actual gaming benchmark and  this time around we got basically double  the performance going from the a14 to  the m1 and yes i'll admit that the  performance is overkill for a lot of the  apps out there right now but this is  actually a good thing for people who  want to buy an ipad and use it for the  next five years knowing that five years  later the m1 is still gonna handle all  the new apps and games that'll be coming  out now while the ipad air 5 still has  the same 64 gigs of storage as before we  actually tested the speed of the storage  and we were surprised to see the read  speeds being 88 faster than before but  the write speeds were actually 3.3 times  faster which is absolutely insane and  this is actually a big deal because it  means all of your apps are going to load  up quicker than before and that in  itself will make it feel more snappy and  to make things even better the usbc port  is now twice as fast 10 gigabits per  second compared to 5 on the previous  model so as far as the performance  aspect we're definitely getting a big  upgrade this time around but then when  we look at the overall design it's  essentially unchanged with the same  chassis size a completely identical  display no changes with the touch of the  power button or anything else we even  tested the speakers and the microphones  and found absolutely zero differences  between the new ipad air and the old one  the rear camera on the back is identical  as well and for some weird reason it  still doesn't come with a flash even  though the less expensive ipad mini 6  does now thankfully the selfie camera  has finally been updated to the 12  megapixel ultrawide camera that all of  the other ipads have been enjoying for  at least the past few months and this  means that you get support for center  stage as well as making face time videos  not look super zoomed in on your face  like it did with the previous ipad air  and then finally the new model now gets  support for optional 5g conductivity so  if you take all of those upgrades and  consider the fact that the 600 price tag  for the new ipad air 5 has not changed  i'd say that this is actually a pretty  good update and compared to an android  tablet you can get this crazy powerful  m1 ipad air 5 with reliable ios and the  jam-packed app store for 600 bucks  instead of paying 700 for the new galaxy  tab s8 which features a two times slower  cpu so the new ipad air is making life  pretty tough for the android tablet  market especially if you consider resale  value which the ipads always excel at  but unfortunately it's not all sunshine  and a daisies for this ipad air review  because it's now time to get into my  frustrations and disappointments and the  first thing i want to begin with is the  usbc port even though the new ipad air  shares the exact same m1 chip as the  ipad pro it still only has a regular 10  gigabit per second usb c port compared  to a 40 gigabit per second thunderbolt  port inside of the ipad pro and the  annoying part about that is that the m1  chip technically comes packed with  thunderbolt controllers so apple is  intentionally slowing down the port on  this ipad air  just to make the ipad pro look better  and what makes it even more annoying is  that we had some pretty exciting leaks  and rumors about the new ipad air coming  with an updated dual camera system with  a square camera bump including a flash  as well as quad stereo speakers and  other improvements but apple decided to  take a completely different route by  simply tossing in the m1 ship as well as  the new selfie camera and then calling  it good which is why i'm calling this a  stop gap update so when we start  comparing the ipad air 5 and the current  ipad pro we start to see just how much  better the ipad pro is in terms of value  first of all the ipad pro costs 200 more  but it gets double the storage so if 64  gigs isn't enough for you on the ipad  air you've got to spend  750 dollars to get a 256 gig model which  is coincidentally the current amazon  sale price for the base 11 inch ipad pro  or better yet you can use the link in  the pinned comment below to get a  renewed 256 gig ipad pro for 765  right now which is an excellent deal but  going further than just the storage  differences the ipad pro has a long list  of advantages for the extra cash like  the fact that it gets a much better quad  stereo speaker system compared to just  dual stereo on this air  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  so as you just heard everything on the  ipad pro is better including the volume  the bass the highs the vocals and the  separation of frequencies but moving on  the ipad pro also has five studio  quality microphones compared to just two  regular mics on the ipad air so listen  to the difference yourself as you guys  can see the ipad air 5 has the new ultra  wide selfie camera which does support  center stage  and the difference between the  microphones is the ipad pro actually has  studio quality microphones and it has  five of them compared to just two so  hopefully you guys can hear a microphone  difference so let me switch over to the  ipad pro here i am on the ipad pro let  me know if there is in fact a microphone  quality difference or not because there  should be because apple advertises it so  yeah also let me know if you see any  difference in the ultrawide cameras  there honestly should not be but there  might so the ipad pro has a huge  advantage in terms of the speakers and  microphone quality but the list does not  end there the ipad pro's display has  thinner bezels and the display itself is  a hundred nits brighter so videos and  movies look better it also comes with  face id authentication which is a major  win compared to the power button touch  id system on the ipad air that isn't  nearly as seamless or reliable and  because of face id the ipad pro supports  portrait mode and memoji features with  the selfie camera it also comes with an  extra ultrawide camera on the back a  flash and the lidar scanner which is  useful for games and ar apps it of  course comes with the thunderbolt port  which is four times faster and it comes  with millimeter wave 5g support while  the air does not get that but the  absolute most important feature of all  is actually the 120hz pro motion display  technology which is exclusive to the  ipad pro and it basically doubles the  refresh rate making swiping through the  ipad and scrolling through apps and  websites look buttery smooth compared to  the choppy 60hz display on the ipad air  now that right there is what i believe  is the most important feature of the  ipad pro because it actually makes your  ipad feel significantly more snappy  while you're using it and if you own the  new iphone 13 pro or you're planning on  buying a pro model iphone in the future  you need to keep in mind that these  iphones support 120 hertz promotion and  take it from me going from a pro motion  iphone to a 60 hertz ipad air is  seriously jarring and you can notice the  lower refresh rate instantly and it's  honestly so annoying and the even bigger  deal is that the 120 hertz refresh rate  allows support for 120 fps gaming which  means that you can actually take full  advantage of the m1 chip's performance  with games like call of duty mobile  running at perfect 120fps which is by  far the most important thing when it  comes to staying competitive in a  shooter game and then other games like  league of legends wild rift and gentian  impact ran at around 100 to 120 fps on  the ipad pro which is very impressive  but on the new ipad air 5 with the same  m1 chip you're literally limited to 60  fps no matter what because the display  has a 60 hertz refresh rate so i  honestly don't even see the point of the  m1 chip when it comes to gaming because  the old a14 ship handled 60 fps just  fine but moving on to the other  advantages of the ipad pro's 120 hertz  promotion support it actually allows the  refresh rate to adapt to your content so  when you're watching a 24 fps movie the  display slows down to 24 hertz which  helps save battery life compared to the  ipad air which is always stuck at 60  hertz and then finally pro motion also  significantly reduces the latency of the  apple pencil on the ipad pro compared to  the ipad air so if you take all of those  advantages including doubling the  storage then i'd say that if there is  any way you can possibly get your hands  on another 150  to buy the ipad pro on sale instead of  the new ipad air 5 then absolutely do it  because you will not regret it and you  won't feel like your m1 ship is being  limited by the 60hz refresh rate of the  ipad air but if you don't own a pro  model iphone and you don't really care  about the 120hz refresh rate then sure  go ahead and save the cash and just buy  the new ipad air 5 because it's still a  great deal compared to the previous ipad  air but now the last thing i want to  mention is the future ipad air model  which i think is coming in around a year  and a half in the fall of 2023 and i  believe that the ipad air 6 will be the  first ipad to use a new oled display  which has been leaked and rumored in  apple's supply chain for a while now so  if you can wait until the end of 2023  then that will actually be a pretty nice  upgrade in terms of display quality as  well as other upgrades like the m2 chip  and more so with that said hopefully you  enjoyed this ipad air 5 review and if  you did click that circle above to  subscribe for more videos like this one  and definitely check out our comparisons  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

